{{Quote|I took in the sunrises off the southern gas marshes and fished the shores of Lake Haruuni, which is so high in the mountains that the fish practically ''float'' out of the water.|Azita Cruuz|<ref name="Mace Windu 3" />}}
'''Lake Haruuni''' was a [[Water|lake]] located high in the [[mountain]]s of<ref name="Mace Windu 3" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="Force Users">{{EncyclopediaCite|Mace Windu and Other Users of the Force}}</ref> [[Haruun Kal]]. Due to its altitude, the [[fish]] that dwelt in the lake practically floated out of its dark waters when the Haruun Kal [[Homeworld|native]] [[Azita Cruuz]] [[Fisher|fished]] for them alone from Lake Haruuni's rocky shores during her [[Youngling|childhood]]. As an adult, Cruuz mentioned fishing at the lake to [[Jedi Knight]] [[Mace Windu]] when the pair [[Mission to Ro Mira|met]] on the [[moon]] [[Ro Mira]]<ref name="Mace Windu 3" /> by [[48 BBY]].<ref name="Date">[[Mace Windu 3|''Mace Windu'' 3]] establishes its events take place prior to [[Mace Windu]]'s entry into the [[Jedi High Council]]. ''[[Master & Apprentice]]'' establishes that Windu is part of the Jedi Council at the [[time]] of [[Nim Pianna]]'s [[Mutiny on the Advent|death]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[48 BBY]]. Therefore, the events of ''Mace Windu'' 3 must take place by that [[Standard year|year]].</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Lake Haruuni appeared in a flashback in the [[Mace Windu 3|third issue]] of the [[2024]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] miniseries ''[[Star Wars: Mace Windu]]''. The issue was written by [[Marc Bernardin]], illustrated by [[Georges Jeanty]], and published by [[Marvel Comics]]<ref name="Mace Windu 3" /> on [[April 17]], 2024.<ref name="Marvel">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/110344/star_wars_mace_windu_2024_3|text=Star Wars: Mace Windu (2024) #3}}</ref>

